<title>UK: Lambert Howarth boosted by upbeat statement.</title>
<headline>Lambert Howarth boosted by upbeat statement.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Lambert Howarth Group Plc, a manufacturer and distributor of footwear and homeware products, rose 16 percent on Thursday after a positive trading statement, dealers said.</p>
<p>The stock was up 19p at 136-1/2 by 1023 GMT in thin volume of 8,100 shares.</p>
<p>The company said trading in the first half of 1997 had been stronger than expected. It expected first-half results to be announced in September 1997 would show a &quot;very significant increase&quot; in profits.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
</text>
